out the f sock designations um  you know one of my concerns has always  been that sippy designations create the  expectations of a taxpayer bailout  should a problem occur  in a way it designates the the firms  that are so designated as too big to  fail  um interestingly um  certain categories of financial  institutions have not been designated  and it occurs to me that certain  business models are inherently  less of a risk to our financial system  for instance asset managers that simply  hold assets on behalf of investors as  opposed to banks  that intermediate credit and transform  maturity  um so asset managers have not been  designated as siffies  thus far do you agree with the decision  that's been made  not to designate at the managers at  sippy's thus far  well when i served on f soccer's fed  chair  um it was proposed to look at  activities that asset managers engage in  that might pose systemic risks and  a paper was issued that um  mentioned problems of possibly  looking at high leverage and hedge funds  a working group was  formed that  was to look at i think it's since been  disbanded  the matter of whether or not  some hedge funds have dangerous levels  of leverage  um open-end mutual funds that promise  daily redemption and liquidity that  invest  in um assets that  are relatively illiquid can pose  problems uh and i think we saw some of  those problems  in march uh  foreign  one two  and i would point out that the money  market funds have been remarkably stable  and  successful but i appreciate that and  look forward to working with you on  these and other issues thank you mr  chairman thank you senator toomey and uh  is senator menendez back i'm being told  that he has not been able to make it  back and so that will conclude the  questioning  dr yellen you've made it through to the  end of the hearing  i know this was a long day for you and  and  we appreciate the fact that you are  willing to serve that  we congratulate you on your nomination  and 